title ALES15 — Lotus's stereo transport, one head reading two channels
prompt Autonomous loop past REMEMBER + the itineraries — keep taking the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment, stop at the custody gates.
think ALES13 (meter) and ALES14 (loop) sent GREEN to both remotes. Next lap, crux-first: two arcs had been diverging — the read side (play ALES7, meter ALES13, loop ALES14) over a MONO master, and the stereo side (pan ALES10, power ALES11, crossfade ALES12) rendering stereo masters nothing ever PLAYED. The durable convergence the whole stereo half pointed at is a stereo transport.
think The crux: one head reads both channels in lockstep, because ALES10's StereoClip invariant is left.len == right.len — the two channels are one master heard twice. So no second cursor and no per-channel bookkeeping: a single position advances through both channels at once. The correctness beyond running ALES7 twice is the lockstep — both channels advance by the same count every block, so left and right never drift out of sample alignment.
think Reused ALES7's Transport head whole (imported, no new cursor type), and proved the read side meets the stereo side directly: a StereoClip rendered by ALES11's power.render_stereo (a center pan, 0.707 per side) plays back its two channels exactly through the new head.
obs GREEN on the first build across six selftest blocks: fixed blocks concatenate back to EACH channel byte-for-byte with left/right aligned; at_end exact over an empty and a played master; mismatched out buffers refuse BadBlock; seek_ms/elapsed_ms round-trip 3ms and a seek to 7ms past a 6-sample master refuses PastEnd; a power-rendered center pan reads back 700/700; a replay after rewind reads identical bytes, the stereo unmutated.
obs No downstream churn — stereo_transport.rye imports transport/pan/clock/timeline (and track/fader/power in the render-playback block) over public APIs only; nothing else touched. Purely local, every custody gate untouched.
loom witness=ales_stereo_transport_witness result=GREEN rung=ALES15 selftest_blocks=6 first_build=GREEN
file lotus/stereo_transport.rye ALES15 — one Transport head over a pan.StereoClip; read_block copies both channels in lockstep (BadBlock on unequal out buffers); at_end / seek_ms / elapsed_ms over the shared length.
file tools/ales_stereo_transport_witness.rish witness proving the stereo transport GREEN — lockstep concat, at_end, BadBlock, seek round-trip/PastEnd, power-rendered playback, read-only.
file active-designing/20260814-fill-ales15-lotus-stereo-transport.md the self-approved design capture for the round.
file lotus/README.md front door synced — ALES15 in the status line, the rung prose, the prove block, and the road-on.
recommend keep-going — the next Lotus rung (metering a stereo master during playback, looping a stereo region, a scrub window, or a punch region tying playback back to the Mikrophone) is mechanical and single-module, policy already written; custody gates all still untouched.
